---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import PixelArt from '../components/PixelArt.astro';
import { GAME, SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About and credits" description="About Super Mario Bros. Crossover: REMIX, a tribute to Jay Pavlina's original, with credits and the fan-project disclaimer.">
  <PageBanner title="About and credits" intro="A love letter to a 2010 fan game, rebuilt for today's browsers." />
  <div class="wrap prose-wide">
    <section aria-labelledby="tribute">
      <h2 id="tribute"><PixelArt name="star" scale={2} /> A tribute</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 2010 Jay Pavlina and Exploding Rabbit released <cite>Super Mario Bros. Crossover</cite>, a free Flash game that
        let you play Super Mario Bros. as Mega Man, Link, Samus, Simon Belmont and other NES heroes, each with their own
        moves. It was a brilliant idea, and beautifully made.
      </p>
      <p>
        Flash is gone, and with it the easy way to play. <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is a from-scratch remake for modern
        browsers and phones that carries the idea forward: a story, a world map, a themed world and a mini game for every
        hero, and a new hero, the tank Sophia III. It is a different project from the original, made with respect and
        thanks. The level layouts come from the original game's open-source release (MIT licensed, no art or sound).
      </p>
      <p>
        Go and see where it started: <a href="https://github.com/JayPavlina/super-mario-bros-crossover">the original
        Super Mario Bros. Crossover source on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="credits">
      <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
      <dl class="credits panel">
        <dt>Original game</dt>
        <dd><cite>Super Mario Bros. Crossover</cite> by Jay Pavlina, Exploding Rabbit (2010)</dd>
        <dt>Remake</dt>
        <dd>Made by jelloshooter848. Code, pixel art and chiptune music are original to the SMBC project.</dd>
        <dt>This website</dt>
        <dd>
          Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on GitHub Pages.{' '}
          Clips and screenshots are captured from the remake itself.{' '}
          <a href={`https://github.com/${SITE.siteRepo}`}>Site source on GitHub</a>.
        </dd>
        <dt>Fonts</dt>
        <dd>
          Press Start 2P by CodeMan38 and Atkinson Hyperlegible by the Braille Institute, both under the SIL Open Font
          License.
        </dd>
        <dt>Forum</dt>
        <dd>GitHub Discussions, embedded with <a href="https://giscus.app">giscus</a>.</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="original-art">
      <h2 id="original-art">All-original art and music</h2>
      <p>
        The remake contains no Nintendo, Capcom, Konami or other third-party art, music or code. Every sprite and tile is
        original pixel art drawn in an NES style, and all music is original chiptune synthesized in your browser.
        Character and game names are used only to describe gameplay styles. The game's code and original assets are
        released under the MIT license; see the <a href={GAME.repoUrl}>game repository</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="disclaimer" class="panel panel--gold">
      <h2 id="disclaimer">Fan project disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is a free, non-commercial fan project. It is <strong>not affiliated with or endorsed by</strong>{' '}
        Nintendo, Capcom, Konami, Tecmo / Koei Tecmo, Sunsoft or Exploding Rabbit. Super Mario Bros., The Legend of Zelda,
        Mega Man, Metroid, Castlevania, Ninja Gaiden, Contra, Blaster Master and all related characters and names are
        trademarks of their respective owners. The remake's code and original art are by the SMBC project.
      </p>
      <p>Nothing here is for sale, and there are no ads. If a rights holder has a concern, please open an issue on the game's repository.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy">
      <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Your browser asks GitHub for the latest release and, on pages with
        comments, loads giscus from giscus.app. The game keeps its save files and settings in your own browser.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-wide {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .credits dt {
    font-family: var(--font-pixel);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .credits dt:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .credits dd {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
  }
  #disclaimer {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  section + section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
